{"item_id": "feed:https://www.treelinereview.com/gearreviews/best-womens-rain-boots", "version_id": "8f101ae52afcbdf84cb5b62b856bf5eb774f8104d77dc3e4c7d87fb8f059ff72", "decision": "reject", "reason": "Under the relevance rules, this is a rain boot roundup aimed at everyday women's wear, not Mammoth competitor gear in the in-scope categories; the boots are footwear for urban and farm use, with no hiking-load or multi-day carry evidence tied to Mammoth conditions. The article is affiliate-supported and its strongest claims (waterproofness, durability) rest on the reviewer's own long-term use rather than the multi-publisher corroboration the credibility and uncertainty rules require, so it does not meet the bar even as a relevant source.", "piece_ids": []}
{"item_id": "feed:https://www.treelinereview.com/gearreviews/1up-usa-heavy-duty-hitch-bike-rack-review", "version_id": "ce44d164860815fb30eac2367a8fc416cdb81bd1c8b34316c08a203b7fa2af04", "decision": "reject", "reason": "Under the relevance rules, a hitch-mounted bike rack is outside every in-scope gear category and is unrelated to Mammoth's on-foot carry conditions. The article is also affiliate-supported, and the \"Similar bike racks\" comparisons and upgrade pricing do not add any Mammoth-relevant evidence.", "piece_ids": []}
{"item_id": "feed:https://www.treelinereview.com/gearreviews/best-ski-boot-bags", "version_id": "9143ede1f8dfe920be515af2a69b29449d39309124381491e14bccc02f983a55", "decision": "reject", "reason": "Under the relevance rules, ski boot bags for winter travel fall outside the in-scope gear categories and do not address carrying loads on foot at Mammoth. The article is affiliate-supported and the tested claims concern airport and road-trip travel rather than endurance carry, so it has no connection to Mammoth conditions.", "piece_ids": []}
